It could be, so long as there was an upper limit on score for non-
ascensions, and all ascensions were worth more than that.  For instance, 
each minor accomplishment (Reaching Minetown, finding the Quest portal, etc) 
could be worth a few points, all the way up to 99 points for offering the 
Amulet on the wrong altar.  Then a basic no-conducts ascension would be 100 
points, with conducts (speed is a conduct of sorts, just not one the game 
currently tracks) increasing that according to some formula.

> After all, how _do_ you
> compare a speed ascension of a dwarven valkyrie with a tourist
> extinctionist?

Easily, since extinctionism doesn't involve much skill.

Comparing actual skill-testing conducts is a little tricky, but you 
basically try to make a good formula that weighs them all fairly.


